{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:15be7b86643c6d313008012cf6bbccb397b26b740de9643e1137481e245f88ae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fd8dcc444af45bea08fbb8404ac414ea585023caf7a6a24c6b7a33547bfe6b0a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus we see that <MATH_0001> is flat if and only if\nthe structure sheaf <MATH_0002> is flat over <MATH_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e443f7a9f31dbbc259cd80b5c7de2b005c1ac36d101ae65a786ad0008ecb14c", "unit_id": "tag:01U2:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0008": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0011": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} V_j$", "MATH_0012": "$f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup_{i \\in I_j} U_i$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0014": "$V_j$", "MATH_0015": "$j\\in J, i\\in I_j$", "MATH_0016": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} V_j$", "MATH_0017": "$f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup_{i \\in I_j} U_i$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{F}(U_i)$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V_j)$", "MATH_0020": "$j\\in J, i\\in I_j$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0022": "$S$", "MATH_0023": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0024": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0025": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{F}|_U$", "MATH_0027": "$V$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-module-characterize}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:88bc42f172e4765cb62068171fab83bc7c4f6808c90a0d653891452949c3174d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f3a184b78773e982f9d42f11f9e6e50e724f43f54fceb85031474483c77f8d2b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The sheaf <MATH_0004> is flat over <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine opens <MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007>\nwith <MATH_0008> the <MATH_0009>-module <MATH_0010> is flat.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an open covering <MATH_0011>\nand open coverings <MATH_0012> such\nthat each of the modules <MATH_0013> is\nflat over <MATH_0014>, for all <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0016>\nand affine open coverings <MATH_0017> such\nthat <MATH_0018> is a flat <MATH_0019>-module, for all\n<MATH_0020>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0021> is flat over <MATH_0022> then for\nany open subschemes <MATH_0023>, <MATH_0024> with <MATH_0025>\nthe restriction <MATH_0026> is flat over <MATH_0027>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dd288a954ca5ddb320ef69b98122db0bf02f2d0852852e3b85b548f40e98ebae", "unit_id": "tag:01U4:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$M$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0007": "$M_{\\mathfrak q}$", "MATH_0008": "$R_{\\mathfrak p}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0010": "$R$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0012": "$M_{\\mathfrak q}$", "MATH_0013": "$R_{\\mathfrak p}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0015": "$A$", "MATH_0016": "$M$", "MATH_0017": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-flat-localization}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bbacc6c4b4e9835f804bdc24b82bbe82095b892444003f88de7403a20ff03f80", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9531c09e41f94381ec4ec9624c0b631e3988e35a956e629514843e766ba87669", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map. Let <MATH_0002> be an <MATH_0003>-module.\nIf <MATH_0004> is <MATH_0005>-flat, then for all primes\n<MATH_0006> the module <MATH_0007> is flat over <MATH_0008>\nwith <MATH_0009> the prime of <MATH_0010> lying under <MATH_0011>. Conversely, if\n<MATH_0012> is flat over <MATH_0013> for all primes <MATH_0014>\nof <MATH_0015>, then <MATH_0016> is flat over <MATH_0017>. See\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThis equivalence easily implies the statements of the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3796bac3b0085a788c37c21d13f1585eb4ee6b05fc418ab77333e6892ea48be9", "unit_id": "tag:01U4:proof"}
